src.cam.exort — v2 single-bundle CAM hook-up (created 2026-07-06)
==================================================================

The ExoRT v2 bundle for CESM1.2.1/ExoCAM (CAM4 physics). Supersedes
src.cam.n68equiv, src.cam.n84equiv, AND src.cam.n68equiv.haze in one
directory: 84-band grid (n84 supersedes n68 via the runtime band
optimizer), 8 major gas species (H2O CO2 CH4 C2H6 NH3 CO O2 O3) plus
N2/H2 CIA, H2O clouds (MCICA), CO2 ice clouds, CARMA haze, and surface
emissivity. The old bundles are kept as frozen legacy connections to
existing ExoCAM setups; do not mix files between them and this bundle.

Gas k-tables are pinned exactly as the validated 1-D build: H2O/CO2/CH4/
C2H6 = HITRAN-2016, NH3/CO = HITRAN-2024, O2/O3 = HITRAN-2020 (see
tests/regression/EXORT_H16_EQUIVALENCE.md). The 1-D regression suite
(15/15, Δ=0) gates the shared solver files in this bundle.

NOT YET RUN IN 3-D. This bundle compiles against a stubbed CESM
environment (all four CPP combinations) but has not yet been compiled or
run inside a real ExoCAM case. First 3-D validation should compare a
clear-sky aquaplanet against an identical src.cam.n68equiv case
(differences should be only the n68->n84 stellar UV regrid, <0.4% SW;
LW bit-close).


Basic usage (mainline configs: cam_aqua_fv, cam_land_fv, ...)
-------------------------------------------------------------
1. Edit sys_rootdir.F90 in this directory: point exort_rootdir at an
   ExoRT checkout on the v2 data layout (data/kdist/<gas>/,
   data/stellar/, data/cloud/, data/aerosol/). The refactor branch, not
   v1/main.

2. Update the config's ExoCAM SourceMods (see "Required ExoCAM changes").

3. Point the case at this bundle:
     xmlchange CAM_CONFIG_OPTS="-nlev XX -phys cam4 \
         -usr_src $EXORT_PATH/ExoRT/3dmodels/src.cam.exort"

Optional physics paths are opt-in at compile time via -cppdefs in
CAM_CONFIG_OPTS:

  macro              enables            requires (ExoCAM side)
  -----------------  -----------------  --------------------------------
  (none)             H2O clouds only    mainline configs (like the old
                                        src.cam.n68equiv)
  -DEXORT_CO2CLD     CO2 ice cloud RT   co2condense config:
                                        exo_condense_mod (CICEWP_CO2 /
                                        REI_CO2 pbuf fields) +
                                        do_exo_condense_co2 flag
  -DEXORT_CARMA      CARMA haze RT      carma config: carma_exort_mod +
                                        CARMA microphysics
                                        (carma_model_mod NELEM/NBIN must
                                        equal radgrid nelem_carma/
                                        nbin_carma = 1/40; checked with
                                        endrun at init)
  -DEXORT_SRF_EMISS  cam_in%srf_emiss   camsrfexch/coupler srf_emiss
                     -> RT emissivity   modifications (currently in the
                                        co2condense config)

Example (Mars co2condense):
     xmlchange CAM_CONFIG_OPTS="... -usr_src .../src.cam.exort \
         -cppdefs '-DEXORT_CO2CLD -DEXORT_SRF_EMISS'"


Required ExoCAM changes (ALL configs that build this bundle)
------------------------------------------------------------
The shared driver (exo_radiation_mod.F90) gates its cloud and haze
kernels on two new exoplanet_mod flags. Add to
SourceMods/src.share/exoplanet_mod.F90:

    !! v2 ExoRT (src.cam.exort) kernel gates
    logical, public, parameter :: do_exo_clouds = .true.          ! H2O cloud RT
    logical, public, parameter :: do_exo_haze   = do_carma_exort  ! haze RT iff CARMA runs

(do_exo_clouds = .true. reproduces the old bundles' always-on cloud
behavior. In configs without do_carma_exort — e.g. circumbinary — set
do_exo_haze = .false. .)

Also update the stellar spectrum path for the v2 layout and 84-band grid:

    exo_solar_file = '<ExoRT>/data/stellar/G2V_SUN_n84.nc'    ! was data/solar/*_n68.nc

An _n84 file is REQUIRED (initialize_solar reads ntot_wavlnrng=84 bins).
All *_n68 files have _n84 counterparts in data/stellar/.

No changes to the exo_radiation_tend call: its argument list is the
frozen ExoRT<->ExoCAM contract and is identical to the old bundles.


Differences from the old bundles (behavior notes)
-------------------------------------------------
- aerad_driver call sites use the v2 optional keyword tail; clear-sky
  companion calls simply OMIT the condensed-phase arguments (no more
  *_zero array fabrication).
- Haze optics are loaded by ExoRT itself (initialize_hazeopts, from
  data/aerosol/haze_n84_b40_*.nc, selected in cloud.F90). ExoCAM's
  carma_exort_optics_init is NOT called; only carma_exort_get_mmr is
  used. NOTE: the committed n84 haze tables are provisional above band
  68 (UV extended from band 68) pending regeneration from
  data/aerosol/refractive_indices/.
- The haze tau kernel uses the driver's coldens layer convention (rad
  layer k <- atmos layer k-1); the old .haze bundle's off-by-one
  (bottom rad level never filled) is fixed (maintainer-confirmed
  2026-07-01).
- The part_in_tshadow `do camtop=` copy-paste bug carried by the old
  bundles is fixed in this bundle's exo_radiation_mod.F90.
- CO2 ice cloud RT: band-indexed kernel, cloud fraction = 1, no MCICA;
  condensate (CICEWP_CO2, g/m2) and particle size (REI_CO2, microns)
  come from the co2condense pbuf fields. With do_exo_condense_co2
  = .false. in a -DEXORT_CO2CLD build, zero-opacity fallbacks are used.
- MCICA H2O-cloud permute seed = get_nstep(), as before (the 1-D
  per-column-seed namelist flag does not exist on the CAM path).
- initialize_cldopts additionally reads rel_grid/rei_grid from the H2O
  optics files and the CO2 ice optics (radii/Qext/W/G) from
  data/cloud/cloudoptics_co2_ice_mie_n84.nc (rei_co2_grid has no
  compiled-in fallback).

Maintenance
-----------
This bundle is a derived artifact of source/ (see
tools/populate3Dmodels.py; `check --exort` must PASS). The only
bundle-local files are sys_rootdir.F90 (machine path) and this README.
A compile-check harness against stubbed CESM modules (all CPP
combinations) is described in REFACTOR_LOG.md under the 2026-07-06
entry.
